            "answer": {
              "short": "$N$ = novel, $S$ = science book. First draw: $P(N)=\\frac{12}{21}$, $P(S)=\\frac{9}{21}$. After $N$: $P(N)=\\frac{11}{20}$, $P(S)=\\frac{9}{20}$. After $S$: $P(N)=\\frac{12}{20}$, $P(S)=\\frac{8}{20}$.",
              "worked": "Without replacement, 20 books remain for the second draw. Reduce the number of the type selected first by one. Multiply along each path:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(NN)&=\\frac{12}{21}\\times\\frac{11}{20}=\\frac{11}{35}\\\\P(NS)&=\\frac{12}{21}\\times\\frac{9}{20}=\\frac{9}{35}\\\\P(SN)&=\\frac{9}{21}\\times\\frac{12}{20}=\\frac{9}{35}\\\\P(SS)&=\\frac{9}{21}\\times\\frac{8}{20}=\\frac{6}{35}.\\end{align*}$$",
