                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The first book is replaced before the second book is selected. Find the probability that both books are the same type.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{25}{49}$",
          "worked": "Same type means two novels or two science books. These outcomes are mutually exclusive.\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(\\text{same type})&=P(NN)+P(SS)\\\\&=\\frac{12}{21}\\times\\frac{12}{21}+\\frac9{21}\\times\\frac9{21}\\\\&=\\frac{16}{49}+\\frac9{49}\\\\&=\\frac{25}{49}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q7-root-bank-p45-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p45-q7-root-bank-4fe01b04-3581-445d-8df4-5b018fde51ed",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The first book is not replaced before the second book is selected. Find the probability that both books are the same type.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{17}{35}$",
          "worked": "Without replacement, 20 books remain for the second draw.\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(\\text{same type})&=P(NN)+P(SS)\\\\&=\\frac{12}{21}\\times\\frac{11}{20}+\\frac9{21}\\times\\frac8{20}\\\\&=\\frac{11}{35}+\\frac6{35}\\\\&=\\frac{17}{35}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q7-root-bank-p45-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p45-q7-root-bank-44cbe498-7fb9-4c33-822d-5d736113b18d",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Find the increase in the probability of selecting two books of different types when the first book is not replaced, compared with when it is replaced. Give the absolute difference between the two probabilities.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac6{245}$",
          "worked": "Different types means a novel then a science book, or a science book then a novel.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Without replacement: }&\\frac{12}{21}\\times\\frac9{20}+\\frac9{21}\\times\\frac{12}{20}=\\frac9{35}+\\frac9{35}=\\frac{18}{35}\\\\\\text{With replacement: }&\\frac{12}{21}\\times\\frac9{21}+\\frac9{21}\\times\\frac{12}{21}=\\frac{12}{49}+\\frac{12}{49}=\\frac{24}{49}\\end{aligned}$$\nUse a common denominator of 245.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{18}{35}-\\frac{24}{49}&=\\frac{126}{245}-\\frac{120}{245}\\\\&=\\frac6{245}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
